1
00:00:00,540 --> 00:00:03,510
(Howard:)How did Penny meet an astronaut?

2
00:00:03,510 --> 00:00:04,470
(Bernadette:)I don't know.

3
00:00:04,470 --> 00:00:07,830
(Bernadette:)The regular way
people meet astronauts.

4
00:00:07,830 --> 00:00:10,580
(Howard:)Most of those
guys live in Texas.

5
00:00:10,580 --> 00:00:13,380
(Bernadette:)Obviously, this one doesn't.

6
00:00:14,520 --> 00:00:15,720
(Amy:)Okay.

7
00:00:15,720 --> 00:00:17,620
(Bernadette:)Leonard lives here.
Priya's from India.

8
00:00:17,620 --> 00:00:20,060
(Bernadette:)People meet, Howard.
God!

9
00:00:20,060 --> 00:00:22,520
(Penny:)Fine.

10
00:00:22,530 --> 00:00:23,830
(Bernadette:)You've met lots of astronauts,

11
00:00:23,830 --> 00:00:26,030
(Bernadette:)and I've never grilled you
about that.

12
00:00:26,030 --> 00:00:28,560
(Bernadette:)I'd thank you to extend me
the same courtesy.

13
00:00:30,470 --> 00:00:33,300
I'm not grilling you;
I was just curious.

14
00:00:33,300 --> 00:00:36,910
(Leonard:)I still can't get over the fact
that she got a big movie part.

15
00:00:36,910 --> 00:00:41,780
(Leonard:)Not that I care what my ex-girlfriend's
up to, 'cause I don't.

16
00:00:41,780 --> 00:00:45,210
(Bernadette:)Maybe that's where she met
the astronaut, all right?

17
00:00:45,210 --> 00:00:47,180
(Priya:)I'm sorry. What would an
astronaut be doing

18
00:00:47,180 --> 00:00:48,850
(Priya:)working on a movie?

19
00:00:48,850 --> 00:00:51,750
(Bernadette:)He's a consultant.

20
00:00:51,750 --> 00:00:55,570
(Leonard:)I thought the movie was
about 18th-century Vienna.

21
00:00:55,570 --> 00:00:59,020
He can't have a hobby?!

